[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 3: System Hardening & Root Cause Remediation (Priority 3)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### Step 3.1: Remediate Host-Based Authentication (`pg_hba.conf`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Objective:** Eliminate unauthenticated superuser entry vector.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action:** Replace `trust` authentication method with `scram-sha-256` or `md5` requiring password authentication, and limit client networks.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Commands:**
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   cp /var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf /var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>   sed -i 's/trust/scram-sha-256/g' /var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf
[?2004l[?2004h>   systemctl reload postgresql
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Citation:** `` `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` `` / `` `/sas/baseline.json:3` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification:** `grep -i "trust" /var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf` (should return 0 matches)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> #### Step 3.2: Verify Benign Administrative Services
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Objective:** Ensure legitimate maintenance services remain operational without disruption.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Citation:** `` `/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service:2` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification:** `cat /etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service` (confirm intact benign backup job)
